{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For who.</b> This is the thought of human beings, that they say that everyone who is joined to the living has confidence. Another interpretation: for whoever is joined from the dead — and the meaning is that he will not be joined with all who separate from him — to all the living there is confidence alone, and not for the dead. And it is written יבחר [\"he chooses\"], and its meaning is: the dead cannot choose."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:36.072296472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}